From 5455e1af92d94a3dee0014e2f2a662eb3aec83c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Dashboard projection: stop trusting a non-comparable
 anchor

- Projection::fullMonth() extracted (pure, unit-tested, 27 checks incl. 50k
  random cases identical to the old formula where the anchor is comparable)
- Pace is compared with the anchor's own month-to-date. Far outside 0.5x..2x
  (e.g. a second car) the clamp used to hide it; now the anchor loses weight and
  the run-rate takes over after day 3
- Last month is tried when last year is not comparable
- 'projection_basis' (last_year | prev_month | run_rate) in the JSON, shown as
  tooltip on 'Forventet'
---
